From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: koyu <me@koyu.space>
Date: Thu, 22 Oct 2026 06:18:55 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 13/15] Add a page that offers to unlock the encrypted disk
 automatically

After the browser page, when the data was encrypted at install time,
offers to have the computer unlock it on start, like BlossomOS'
`ujust tpm enroll`: systemd-cryptenroll --tpm2-device=auto, bound to
PCR 7, with the passphrase kept as a fallback. It is worded as a
convenience, without TPMs or firmware.

It is only offered when /etc/crypttab has a LUKS2 disk without a TPM
unlock yet, systemd can use the TPM 2.0 (systemd-analyze has-tpm2) and
Secure Boot is on; without Secure Boot PCR 7 would unseal the disk for
whatever boots. Otherwise the page skips itself.

Two new helper actions do the root part, which the setup user may run
without asking: one lists the disks to enroll, the other checks the
passphrase on each with cryptsetup and then enrolls them. The disks are
always the helper's own pick, never the caller's. In a preview the page
is always offered and enrolling is pretended.
